# Copy to .env and fill in if you add web-side configuration.
#
# The web app currently needs no environment variables: it talks to the
# server only through src/api/client.ts, which calls relative /api/* paths
# proxied to the server by Vite in dev (see vite.config.ts) and served from
# the same origin in production.
#
# If you add client-side config in future, only variables prefixed
# VITE_ are exposed to the browser bundle. Never put server secrets
# (API keys, database paths, cookie secrets) in a VITE_ variable — the
# bundle check script (scripts/check-bundle.mjs) fails the build if any
# server env var name leaks into the built web bundle.
